{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":3,"query":"name=Drucker&limit=10&title=Managing Oneself","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"Managing oneself","subTitle":"and What makes an effective executive"},"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Drucker, Peter F. (Peter Ferdinand)",{"@type":"date","#text":"1909-2005"}],"role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author."}}]},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"mau"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"Massachusetts"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2017"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Boston, Massachusetts :"}},"publisher":"Harvard Business Review Press,","dateIssued":[2017]}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"x, 107 pages ; 18 cm"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Peter Drucker is widely regarded as the father of modern management, offering penetrating insights into business that still resonate today. But Drucker also offers deep wisdom on how to manage our personal lives and how to become more effective leaders. In these two classic articles from \"Harvard Business Review,\" Drucker reveals the keys to becoming your own chief executive officer as well as a better leader of others. \"Managing Oneself\" identifies the probing questions you need to ask to gain the insights essential for taking charge of your career, while \"What Makes an Effective Executive\" outlines the key behaviors you must adopt in order to lead. Together, they chart a powerful course to help you carve out your place in the world. -- Provided by publisher."},"tableOfContents":"Preface -- Managing oneself -- What makes an effective executive.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Peter F. Drucker."},"\"The key to success\"--Cover.","\"Originally published in Harvard Business Review in March 1999 and June 2004\"--Title page verso.","Includes index.",{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Management"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Leadership"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Success"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"HD31 .D7736 2017"},{"@edition":"23","@authority":"ddc","#text":"650.1"}],"relatedItem":[{"@type":"constituent","titleInfo":{"title":"What makes an effective executive"},"name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Drucker, Peter F. (Peter Ferdinand),",{"@type":"date","#text":"1909-2005"}]}},{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990149131670203941/catalog"}}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9781633693043"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"163369304X"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"959802937"}],"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000123374118","#text":"Baker Library, Harvard Business School, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HD31 .D7736 2017"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000123374118","#text":"Baker Library, Harvard Business School, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HD31 .D7736 2017"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Baker Business"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990149131670203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"014913167"}},"processingDate":"2024-03-26T05:23Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"rda","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"BTCTA"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"160930"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20170227"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990149131670203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)","languageOfCataloging":{"languageTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"}}}},{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":[{"title":"Managing oneself "},{"@type":"uniform","title":"Harvard business review"}],"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Drucker, Peter F. (Peter Ferdinand),",{"@type":"date","#text":"1909-2005"}],"role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"mau"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"Massachusetts"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Boston, Mass"}}],"dateIssued":[{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2008"},"c2008"],"issuance":"monographic","agent":{"namePart":"Harvard Business School Press"}},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"60 p. ; 17 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"With ambition, drive, and talent, you can rise to the top of your chosen profession regardless of where you started out. But companies today aren't managing your career-- you must be your own chief executive officer. It's up to you to carve out your place in the world and know when to change course. In this short work Drucker gives you the keys to unlock your full potential so that you can achieve true and lasting excellence."},